# Meson build trees: the guest cross file and both build dirs are machine-local
build/

# CONTENT NEVER ENTERS THIS REPOSITORY.
#
# A PlayStation needs its ROM, and every disc image that exists is somebody's.
# Everything under tests/roms is ignored WHOLESALE rather than by pattern: a
# rule that lists what may not be committed is a rule that eventually misses
# one. What this repository may ship (a program it builds itself, a test suite
# under a free licence) goes in tests/own/ instead, which is tracked.
tests/roms/
tests/roms-local/
tests/firmware-local/

# the sandbox writes this when a guest faults
minibox-diag.log

# the frontend gate's scratch: configs, logs, RAM dumps and screenshots
waterbox/tests/work/
